    "authorAssociation": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.completion\n\n### Question\n\nHi, first I'm really grateful for what you did in the mini community. I like mini ones very much and mostly used them everyday together with several other necessary ones(lspconfig, treesitter etc.) Really really great!\r\nRecently I switched from `nvim-cmp` to `mini.completion` and `mini.snippets`. With `mini.completion` I was having trouble to set it as expected, especially about several note-taking lsp servers.\r\n\r\nAt present I tried `marksman` and `zk`(`zk-nvim`). Both provide functionality like link completion. I also configured it as noted in the doc. A quick example like below,\r\n\r\n```lua\r\n-- marksman\r\n▒ lspconfig.marksman.setup {\r\n▒   capabilities = capabilities,\r\n▒   on_attach = on_attach,\r\n}\r\n▒\r\n▒ -- zk\r\n▒ require(\"zk\").setup {\r\n▒   picker = \"minipick\",\r\n▒   lsp = {\r\n▒     -- `config` is passed to `vim.lsp.start_client(config)`\r\n▒     config = {\r\n▒     ╎ cmd = { \"zk\", \"lsp\" },\r\n▒     ╎ name = \"zk\",\r\n▒     ╎ on_attach = on_attach,\r\n▒     },\r\n▒\r\n▒     -- automatically attach buffers in a zk notebook that match the given filetypes\r\n▒     auto_attach = {\r\n▒       enabled = true,\r\n▒       filetypes = { \"markdown\" },\r\n▒     },\r\n▒   },\r\n▒ }\r\n```\r\nin `on_attach` I have below setup,\r\n```lua\r\n-- Set up 'mini.completion' LSP part of completion\r\nvim.bo[bufnr].omnifunc = \"v:lua.MiniCompletion.completefunc_lsp\"\r\n```\r\n\r\nBut even with all above, the link completion functionality is not available. I'm not sure it is caused by `mini.completion` or my non-proper setup. But this worked with `nvim-cmp`. Looking forward to any hints and suggestions. Thank you in advance.",
    "bodyHTML": "<h3 dir=\"auto\">Contributing guidelines</h3>\n<ul class=\"contains-task-list\">\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Completed task\" checked=\"\"> I have read <a href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md\">CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Module(s)</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">mini.completion</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Question</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Hi, first I'm really grateful for what you did in the mini community. I like mini ones very much and mostly used them everyday together with several other necessary ones(lspconfig, treesitter etc.) Really really great!<br>\nRecently I switched from <code class=\"notranslate\">nvim-cmp</code> to <code class=\"notranslate\">mini.completion</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">mini.snippets</code>. With <code class=\"notranslate\">mini.completion</code> I was having trouble to set it as expected, especially about several note-taking lsp servers.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">At present I tried <code class=\"notranslate\">marksman</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">zk</code>(<code class=\"notranslate\">zk-nvim</code>). Both provide functionality like link completion. I also configured it as noted in the doc. A quick example like below,</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-lua notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"-- marksman\n▒ lspconfig.marksman.setup {\n▒   capabilities = capabilities,\n▒   on_attach = on_attach,\n}\n▒\n▒ -- zk\n▒ require(&quot;zk&quot;).setup {\n▒   picker = &quot;minipick&quot;,\n▒   lsp = {\n▒     -- `config` is passed to `vim.lsp.start_client(config)`\n▒     config = {\n▒     ╎ cmd = { &quot;zk&quot;, &quot;lsp&quot; },\n▒     ╎ name = &quot;zk&quot;,\n▒     ╎ on_attach = on_attach,\n▒     },\n▒\n▒     -- automatically attach buffers in a zk notebook that match the given filetypes\n▒     auto_attach = {\n▒       enabled = true,\n▒       filetypes = { &quot;markdown&quot; },\n▒     },\n▒   },\n▒ }\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><span class=\"pl-c\"><span class=\"pl-c\">--</span> marksman</span>\n▒ <span class=\"pl-smi\">lspconfig</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">marksman</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">setup</span> {\n▒   <span class=\"pl-smi\">capabilities</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">capabilities</span>,\n▒   <span class=\"pl-smi\">on_attach</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">on_attach</span>,\n}\n▒\n▒ <span class=\"pl-c\"><span class=\"pl-c\">--</span> zk</span>\n▒ <span class=\"pl-c1\">require</span>(<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>zk<span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span></span>).<span class=\"pl-c1\">setup</span> {\n▒   <span class=\"pl-smi\">picker</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>minipick<span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span></span>,\n▒   <span class=\"pl-smi\">lsp</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> {\n▒     <span class=\"pl-c\"><span class=\"pl-c\">--</span> `config` is passed to `vim.lsp.start_client(config)`</span>\n▒     <span class=\"pl-smi\">config</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> {\n▒     ╎ <span class=\"pl-smi\">cmd</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> { <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>zk<span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span></span>, <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>lsp<span class=\"pl-pds\">\" </span></span>},\n▒     ╎ <span class=\"pl-smi\">name</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>zk<span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span></span>,\n▒     ╎ <span class=\"pl-smi\">on_attach</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">on_attach</span>,\n▒     },\n▒\n▒     <span class=\"pl-c\"><span class=\"pl-c\">--</span> automatically attach buffers in a zk notebook that match the given filetypes</span>\n▒     <span class=\"pl-smi\">auto_attach</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> {\n▒       <span class=\"pl-smi\">enabled</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">true</span>,\n▒       <span class=\"pl-smi\">filetypes</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> { <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>markdown<span class=\"pl-pds\">\" </span></span>},\n▒     },\n▒   },\n▒ }</pre></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">in <code class=\"notranslate\">on_attach</code> I have below setup,</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-lua notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"-- Set up 'mini.completion' LSP part of completion\nvim.bo[bufnr].omnifunc = &quot;v:lua.MiniCompletion.completefunc_lsp&quot;\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><span class=\"pl-c\"><span class=\"pl-c\">--</span> Set up 'mini.completion' LSP part of completion</span>\n<span class=\"pl-smi\">vim</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">bo</span>[<span class=\"pl-smi\">bufnr</span>].<span class=\"pl-e\">omnifunc</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>v:lua.MiniCompletion.completefunc_lsp<span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span></span></pre></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">But even with all above, the link completion functionality is not available. I'm not sure it is caused by <code class=\"notranslate\">mini.completion</code> or my non-proper setup. But this worked with <code class=\"notranslate\">nvim-cmp</code>. Looking forward to any hints and suggestions. Thank you in advance.</p>",
    "bodyText": "Contributing guidelines\n\n I have read CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md\n\nModule(s)\nmini.completion\nQuestion\nHi, first I'm really grateful for what you did in the mini community. I like mini ones very much and mostly used them everyday together with several other necessary ones(lspconfig, treesitter etc.) Really really great!\nRecently I switched from nvim-cmp to mini.completion and mini.snippets. With mini.completion I was having trouble to set it as expected, especially about several note-taking lsp servers.\nAt present I tried marksman and zk(zk-nvim). Both provide functionality like link completion. I also configured it as noted in the doc. A quick example like below,\n-- marksman\n▒ lspconfig.marksman.setup {\n▒   capabilities = capabilities,\n▒   on_attach = on_attach,\n}\n▒\n▒ -- zk\n▒ require(\"zk\").setup {\n▒   picker = \"minipick\",\n▒   lsp = {\n▒     -- `config` is passed to `vim.lsp.start_client(config)`\n▒     config = {\n▒     ╎ cmd = { \"zk\", \"lsp\" },\n▒     ╎ name = \"zk\",\n▒     ╎ on_attach = on_attach,\n▒     },\n▒\n▒     -- automatically attach buffers in a zk notebook that match the given filetypes\n▒     auto_attach = {\n▒       enabled = true,\n▒       filetypes = { \"markdown\" },\n▒     },\n▒   },\n▒ }\nin on_attach I have below setup,\n-- Set up 'mini.completion' LSP part of completion\nvim.bo[bufnr].omnifunc = \"v:lua.MiniCompletion.completefunc_lsp\"\nBut even with all above, the link completion functionality is not available. I'm not sure it is caused by mini.completion or my non-proper setup. But this worked with nvim-cmp. Looking forward to any hints and suggestions. Thank you in advance.",
