                    "authorAssociation": "NONE",
                    "body": "maybe a quick update. I tried `blink.cmp`. and it has completion items after setting `require('blink.cmp').get_lsp_capabilities(config.capabilities)` in lspconfig(so no completion items in `mini.completion` may be due to only `vim.bo[bufnr].omnifunc = \"v:lua.MiniCompletion.completefunc_lsp\"` in lsp is not enough? just my guess :)). But I have to say it didn't work very well, either. The problem should come from `zk` lsp server itself. So I now return back to `mini.completion` again. I like its simplicity and pure nature. Maybe I should refer to thread [#826] to learn something about setting up `process_items` in `mini.completion`.",
                    "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">maybe a quick update. I tried <code class=\"notranslate\">blink.cmp</code>. and it has completion items after setting <code class=\"notranslate\">require('blink.cmp').get_lsp_capabilities(config.capabilities)</code> in lspconfig(so no completion items in <code class=\"notranslate\">mini.completion</code> may be due to only <code class=\"notranslate\">vim.bo[bufnr].omnifunc = \"v:lua.MiniCompletion.completefunc_lsp\"</code> in lsp is not enough? just my guess :)). But I have to say it didn't work very well, either. The problem should come from <code class=\"notranslate\">zk</code> lsp server itself. So I now return back to <code class=\"notranslate\">mini.completion</code> again. I like its simplicity and pure nature. Maybe I should refer to thread [<a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"2254568216\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/issues/826\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/issues/826/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/issues/826\">#826</a>] to learn something about setting up <code class=\"notranslate\">process_items</code> in <code class=\"notranslate\">mini.completion</code>.</p>",
                    "bodyText": "maybe a quick update. I tried blink.cmp. and it has completion items after setting require('blink.cmp').get_lsp_capabilities(config.capabilities) in lspconfig(so no completion items in mini.completion may be due to only vim.bo[bufnr].omnifunc = \"v:lua.MiniCompletion.completefunc_lsp\" in lsp is not enough? just my guess :)). But I have to say it didn't work very well, either. The problem should come from zk lsp server itself. So I now return back to mini.completion again. I like its simplicity and pure nature. Maybe I should refer to thread [#826] to learn something about setting up process_items in mini.completion.",
